## Mistakes Log (Boris-pattern)

**Convention:** When the agent does something wrong, add a one-line entry here. Future sessions read this and avoid repeating.

**Format:** `- YYYY-MM-DD — <symptom>. **Correction:** <correction>. **Codified:** <test path / hook / memory file / "not yet">`

The **Codified** field is the prune signal — entries with concrete codification can be pruned once the codification has held for ≥30 days. Entries marked `not yet` stay until codified or stop being relevant.

**Cap:** ~30 active entries. When exceeded, run a consolidation pass — ≥3 entries sharing a root cause collapse into one meta-entry.

### When to add an entry

- Operator corrects the agent
- A test fails on first run because of a wrong assumption
- A "complete" claim turns out to have gaps
- A claim gets contradicted by data on closer inspection

### Don't add for

- Transient errors (network, API timeouts)
- Operator preference shifts (those go in feedback memory)
- Trivial typos

